John Hancock Life Insurance Company (USA)
Job Site:
200 Berkeley Street, Boston, MA 02111
Job Title:
Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer
Job Duties
Design, develop, test, deliver, maintain, and improve business applications as member of team working across full-stack through entire software development lifecycle. Duties include:
Design end-user interfaces, databases, Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) and server-side logic while maintaining both front and back-end web application components;
Apply disciplined coding practices to enable agility and delivery of high-quality code;
Apply design patterns, automation, and semantic versioning where and when available;
Use development frameworks and third-party libraries;
Conduct wide range of tests and analyses to ensure software applications meet or exceed standards and end user requirements;
Develop detailed system design specifications to serve as a guide for system/program development;
Assist with the development of automated test harnesses to ensure delivery of high-quality code;
Perform investigative “spikes” to mitigate technical uncertainties and risks;
Troubleshoot errors, help resolve bugs, and improve overall efficiency of software;
Participate in ideation and brainstorming sessions to devise creative and disruptive digital solutions;
Create prototype designs for products using wide range of techniques;
Complete documentation required for deployments, maintenance, support and business needs; and
Perform peer reviews of code/deliverables and analysis of continuous learning and continuous improvement.
Work Arrangement requirement: Hybrid from Boston Office (3 days from office, 2 days from home).
Minimum Requirements
Master’s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Information Systems, Electronic Engineering or related field and 5 years of experience using Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) 6x.
Experience Must Include The Following, Which May Be Gained Concurrently And May Be Gained Before, During, Or After Master’s Degree
5 years of experience with HTML5, CSS3 and JavaScript;
5 years of Java development experience;
1 year of experience troubleshooting and resolving website accessibility issues;
2 years of experience troubleshooting and resolving performance issues;
1 year of Salesforce Integration experience;
2 years of web design experience;
1 year of experience using CI/DI methods;
1 year of database design experience.
Salary: $178,131 per year
The role being advertised is an existing vacancy.
